    <item>
      <title>Hugo_command_line</title>
      <link>https://thefoolgy.github.io/archetypes/hugo_command_line/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 31 Jan 2025 19:52:35 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://thefoolgy.github.io/archetypes/hugo_command_line/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;There are two ways to create new posts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;hugo new content post/hugo_command_line/index.md
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;It will automatically create file under content directory. However, it is not applicable to papermod theme. I need to move the file to content/archetypes, then it will work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;hugo new --kind post archetypes/post.md 
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This one will automatically generate file under content/archetypes and works well. This command line comes from the papermod&amp;rsquo;s author&amp;rsquo;s wiki. Will investigate on it further.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
